Revision history for ROCm-Inference

0.01  unreleased
    - First version: the libinference C API function by function (load_model, kv_cache_init, tokenize,
      detokenize, generate with streaming callbacks and stop strings, prefill, decode_token, get_logits, ...).
    - Chat: chat_render / chat with the model's own chat template, rendered by the Minijinja module, with
      the Python string/dict methods, tojson and raise_exception that chat templates use; the Qwen3,
      Qwen3.5/3.6 and Qwen3.8 templates render as Python jinja2 does (tools, tool calls, UTF-8 text).
      Needs Minijinja 0.1.1 (callbacks that die abort rendering, boolean returns, character strings).
    - chat splits the reply into reasoning, content and tool calls and returns it as a message for the next
      turn (reasoning_content, tool_calls); on_delta streams it by kind; max_thinking_tokens caps the
      reasoning.
    - bin/rocm-inference-server: an OpenAI-compatible chat server (/v1/chat/completions, streamed as
      server-sent events with reasoning_content and tool_calls) for one model on a unix socket behind nginx,
      built on Web::Route.
    - KV block store: store_open, store_stats, store_block_names; ROCm::Inference::Store for the policy
      (eviction to a size, a disk tier: store_evict, store_spill, store_fetch).
    - Speculative decoding with an MTP draft head (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next): set_draft_model, set_draft_tokens
      (1-3 chained drafts per pass, or adaptive); the output equals decoding without it.
    - set_lm_head_q8 (an int8 copy of a float LM head), set_prefill_batch (tokens per prefill micro-batch;
      2048 by default for MoE models).
    - Gemma-4: chat's reply tags and tool calls in Gemma's format (<|channel>thought ... <channel|>,
      <|tool_call>call:name{...}<tool_call|>), chosen by reply_tags from the model's chat template;
      chat_render leaves out the template's <bos> when tokenize adds one.
    - load_model($path, { stage => $dir }): the GPU tensors staged in a huge-page tmpfs and reused by later
      loads; stage_info; rocm-inference-server --stage. Nemotron-3 (nemotron_h_moe) models.
    - set_kv_type($m, 'q8_0'): a Q8_0 KV cache (half the memory); rocm-inference-server --kv-type.
    - Sequences: seq_new / seq_select / seq_current / seq_free, several conversations on one model, each with
      its own KV cache and state. stream_begin (ROCm::Inference::Stream) and chat_start
      (ROCm::Inference::ChatStream) generate one token per step, so sequences can be interleaved.
    - step_streams / step_chats: one step of several streams / chats in one forward pass (batched decoding,
      about 3.5 times the tokens per second at 8 sequences, the same tokens).
    - rocm-inference-server --parallel N: N conversations at once, all advanced one token per round of the
      server's loop in one forward pass (needs Web::Route's pull responses); a client that leaves frees its
      sequence. A new prompt is prefilled --prefill-chunk tokens (512) per round, so the others go on meanwhile.
    - stream_begin / chat_start option prefill_chunk; ChatStream prompt_tokens.
    - rocm-inference-server defaults for agents (opencode): --ctx is the model's trained context (at most
      131072) instead of 8192; --max_tokens 0 (no limit of its own) instead of a silent cap at 4096: a
      request's max_tokens is honoured, without one a reply runs to its end or the context's.
    - Chat templates are rendered with trim_blocks and lstrip_blocks, as transformers' apply_chat_template
      (Nemotron-3's template depends on them).
    - set_swa_ring / swa_ring: the sliding-window layers' KV cache as a ring (the default) or every layer's
      whole history (0, needed by a block store); rocm-inference-server --swa-ring.
    - Makefile.PL finds libinference through ROCM_INFERENCE_PREFIX, pkg-config (rocm-inference) or the
      rocm-hip checkout it sits in, and exits without a Makefile ("not applicable") when there is none.
